# React & React Native Patterns

## 1. Components

- Arrow components only; give **props** an `interface` / `type` and either **`FunctionComponent<Props>`** or an **explicit return** `: ReactElement` / `: ReactNode` so the tree shape is obvious in signatures.
- **Expo Router**: route files in `src/app/**` use **`export default`** (`const Screen = (): ReactElement => …; export default Screen`). All other UI modules use **named exports**.
- Co-locate **`useScreenName.ts`** (or `useComponentName.ts`) next to heavy screens — UI stays thin, hook holds orchestration.

## 2. React Native UI

- **Styling is NativeWind `className` — only.** NEW/touched code: express **all** static styling with `className`; **never** `StyleSheet.create()`. `hover:` variants are a **no-op on native** — use `active:` / `pressed:` for press feedback (e.g. `active:opacity-80`, as in `ErrorBoundary`). **Narrow carve-out:** inline `style={{ … }}` is allowed ONLY for dynamic values NativeWind cannot express as a class (e.g. `gap: SPACING_TOKENS.lg`, `flex: 1`) — never to rebuild a static stylesheet. Existing inline styles: leave as-is, do not migrate.
- **`Pressable`**, never legacy touchables, for NEW interactive elements (`TouchableOpacity` / `TouchableHighlight` only when a specific legacy behavior demands it).
- **Lists**: for large virtualized lists later, prefer **`@shopify/flash-list`** (add when needed) over naive `ScrollView` of hundreds of rows.
- **Images**: for production lists/thumbnails, prefer **`expo-image`** over raw `Image` when you add that dependency.

## 3. Accessibility (native)

- Set meaningful **`accessibilityLabel`** (and `accessibilityRole` / `accessibilityState`) where visuals are icon-only or non-obvious.
- Loading: `accessibilityState={{ busy: true }}` where applicable; errors: clear text for screen readers.

## 4. Hooks

- Hooks only at the top level of components or other hooks.
- Domain hooks live under `src/hooks/<domain>/` with tests alongside when logic is non-trivial.

## 5. Anti-patterns

- ❌ `FC` alias — use `FunctionComponent`.
- ❌ `import React from 'react'` — not needed with the automatic JSX runtime.
- ❌ Manual `useMemo` / `useCallback` / `React.memo` — **React Compiler is ON** (`experiments.reactCompiler: true`) and auto-memoises pure derivations on each render (see `src/features/todo/useTodoWorkspace.ts`). NEW/touched code: do **NOT** hand-memoise. Add it back ONLY for a specific, confirmed regression; opt a single file out with `'use no memo'` at the top — **never** disable the compiler globally.
- ❌ `StyleSheet.create()` or `hover:` classes in new code — see §2.
- ❌ Business logic **> ~10 lines** inlined in JSX — extract to a hook or helper.
- ❌ Web-only APIs (`window`, `document`, `div`) in shared mobile code.

## 6. Visual quality — avoid the "AI aesthetic"

AI-generated UI has recognizable tells; for any UI work reject the default in favour of the design system / tokens.

- **Use the semantic NativeWind tokens**, never arbitrary colors: `bg-background` / `text-foreground`, `bg-primary` / `text-primary-foreground`, `bg-muted` / `text-muted-foreground`, `border-border`, `bg-destructive`. ❌ `bg-[#7c3aed]` / raw hex / the AI-default indigo-purple.
- **Palette lives in one place** — HSL vars in `global.css` + `colors` in `tailwind.config.js`. Extend there; don't hardcode per-screen. `darkMode` is `class`, so keep `:root` **and** `.dark:root` in sync and check contrast in both.
- **Gradients aren't in the token set** — skip decorative `expo-linear-gradient` washes; use flat token fills unless the design explicitly calls for one.
- **Radius by hierarchy** — stick to the Tailwind scale (`rounded-md`, `rounded-lg`, `rounded-full` for pills) and vary it; don't slap `rounded-3xl` on every card and button.
- **Depth is native and subtle** — Android `elevation` / iOS shadow props via `shadow-*`; prefer `border-border` separation over heavy stacked shadows. No web-style multi-layer box-shadows (they don't translate cleanly to native anyway).
- **Spacing from the scale** — `p-2`…`p-6`, `gap-*` applied with intent; not uniform oversized `p-8` padding on everything.
- **Realistic copy via i18n** — every user-visible string through `t()` / `src/shared/locales/` JSON, never lorem-ipsum or hardcoded English (real strings reveal true wrapping / overflow / length).
- **Content-first layout** — priority-driven, not the generic hero + uniform stock-card grid. Use real lists (`@shopify/flash-list`) and real thumbnails (`expo-image`), not decorative placeholder rows.
